# Workflow: Local Test Execution

Purpose:
   Specify how to execute tests locally in Docker containers for
   SUBTASK, MODULE, and SYSTEM levels using the extended builders
   and test-runner service.

Owns: workflow/local-test-execution.sdd

TestExecution:
   Subtask test:
     docker compose run --rm be-builder npm test -- --testPathPattern="<subtask_scope>"
     docker compose run --rm fe-builder npm test -- --testPathPattern="<subtask_scope>"
     docker compose run --rm mobile-builder npm test -- --testPathPattern="<subtask_scope>"

   Module test:
     docker compose run --rm test-runner ./run-module-tests.sh <module_name>

   System test:
     docker compose run --rm test-runner ./run-system-tests.sh <decision_id>

ScriptLocations:
   run-module-tests.sh: .sdd/codding/scripts/run-module-tests.sh
   run-system-tests.sh: .sdd/codding/scripts/run-system-tests.sh

Rules:
   [LTE1] All test execution MUST run inside Docker ([R102], [W19])
   [LTE2] Test scope MUST match the declared level
   [LTE3] Test results MUST be captured in JUnit/XML format for aggregation
   [LTE4] Coverage reports MUST be generated when applicable
   [LTE5] Test failures MUST halt propagation to higher levels

Navigation:
   DockerCompose: @../../docker-compose.yml
   TestRunner: @Dockerfile.test-runner
   BuilderServices: @be-builder,@fe-builder,@mobile-builder
   TestHierarchy: @../workflow/test-hierarchy.sdd
   MicroUnit: @../workflow/micro-unit.sdd

State: +
   (Local Docker test execution specification)
   (Subtask: builder services, Module/System: test-runner service)
   (All execution in Docker per [R102])